title: Choosing Our Enemies
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1930 and enemies_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; enemies_timer = 18
max-visits: 3
is-card: true
card-image: img/poster_1.png
tags: party_affairs

= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti-democratic_parties: Everyone is our enemy, they've all been consumed by the accelerationists!
- @far_right: The far right - ESN has prevented us from aiding the DSA government during their fight with accelerationism.
- @acc: The Accelerationists alone.
- @left: The Left.
- @bourgeois: The center parties - EPP and Renew.
- @easy_discard

@anti-democratic_parties
choose-if: accelerationism >= 60
unavailable_subtitle: Accelerationism hasn't taken hold... yet.
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic_parties"; girondins_strength -= 5; neodemocrat_strength -= 10; neodemocrat_dissent += 5; workers_left -= 2; workers_epp -= 2; workers_greens -= 2; workers_acc -= 5

Attacking the accelerationists is popular among all but the neodemocrats of our party, who would prefer trying to save the formerly democratic parties from the accelerated. Our messaging seems to appeal to some workers, luckily.

@far_right
on-arrival: enemies = "far right"; neodemocrat_strength += 10; neodemocrat_dissent -= 5; workers_esn -= 4; rural_esn -= 4;

Attacking the far right is popular among the neodemocrats and the entire party, although the leftcons would prefer a more ambiguous tone, currently critical of our lack of response to the Left. Nevertheless, the popularity of the ESN takes a slight hit.

@acc
on-arrival: enemies = "accelerationists"; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_acc -= 4;

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or nsdap_r < 10 : The ACC is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many don't question our decision, due to their domination over 5 continents. ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and acc_r >= 10 : The accelerationists are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. Europa must not fall ?]

@left
on-arrival: enemies = "Left"; regulationists_strength += 15; girondins_dissent += 8; regulationists_dissent -= 5; left_relation -= 15; renew_relation += 1; epp_relation += 3; workers_left -= 4;

Attacking the Left is supported mostly by the regulationists, and wins us a meager amount of approval among the center parties. However, If we are to reconcile with the Left, we may have lost already. The Girondins are not happy with our decision.

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "center parties"; girondins_strength += 8; girondins_dissent -= 5; renew_relation -= 5; epp_relation -= 5; left_relation += 5; regulationist_dissent += 8; workers_epp -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1

Our anti-neoliberal rhetoric is popular among the girondins, but the regulationists and other parties are not thrilled at our message.
